@startuml batch-states
' BatchExecutionStatus (core) values confirmed unchanged: RUNNING, COMPLETED,
' FAILED, SKIPPED.
[*] --> RUNNING : runJob() [scheduler, quando isDue()]\n/ triggerManually() [POST /api/batch/schedules/{id}/trigger]
RUNNING --> COMPLETED : jobOperator.start(forecastJob, ...) concluído\nsem excepção (springBatchJobExecutionId gravado)
RUNNING --> FAILED : excepção lançada por jobOperator.start(...)\n(errorMessage gravado)
note right of RUNNING
  SKIPPED is defined in BatchExecutionStatus but is not currently produced
  anywhere in BatchScheduleService — a BatchExecution is only ever created
  in the RUNNING state. A manual trigger while one is already RUNNING is
  rejected up front with a 400 BadRequestException
  ("error.batch.already.running") before any BatchExecution row is
  created, rather than recording a SKIPPED execution.
end note
COMPLETED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
@enduml
